{title: Struck Down at Helam}
{subtitle: 2 Samuel 10:15–16; 10:16–17; 10:17–18; 10:18; 10:19; 1 Chronicles 19:16–19}
{key: Bbm}
{tempo: 78}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bbm] | [Bbm] | [Bbm] | [Gb] |
| [Gb] | [Ebm7] | [Ebm7] | [Bbm] |
| [Bbm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Arameans saw they had been defeated
They re[Gb]grouped in the shadow of the field
[Ebm7]Hadadezer sent out his messengers
To pull [Bbm]the soldiers from beyond the river
They came to Helam in a heavy line
[Gb]With Shobach leading them, commander of the fight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
When [Ebm7]David was told of this new threat
He [Bbm]gathered all Israel, strong and set
Crossed the Jordan to meet them face to face
The [Gb]Arameans drew up their lines in place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Shobach [Bbm]fell where the battle raged
Struck down [Gb]by the hand of David's might
He died [Ebm7]there in the dust and the blood
The commander of their [Bbm]army, no more stood
The Arameans fled before Israel's power
And the vassal kings bowed to the hour
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gb]Seven hundred charioteers were slain [Bbm]
Forty thousand horsemen gone in vain
[Gb]The resistance broke, the fear was deep
[Ebm]The kings who served Hadadezer had to sleep
They [Bbm]made peace with the people of the land
Subject now to a foreign hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Gb]The fear took hold, they dared not stand
To [Ebm]help the Ammonites across the land
The [Bbm]alliance broke, the war was done
Under the rule of the chosen son
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Shobach fell where [Gb]the battle raged
Struck down by the hand [Bbm]of David's might
He died there in the [Gb]dust and the blood
The commander of [Ebm]their army, no more stood
The Arameans fled before [Bbm]Israel's power
And the vassal kings bowed to the hour
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
No longer willing to help the foe
The army [Gb]of Hadadezer is low
Shobach [Bbm]is gone, [Gb]the battle is past
[Ebm]Only the truth of this [Bbm]day will last
{end_of_verse}

